AWS Security Services:- 

1. Monitoring, Logging & Auditing :-

	1. Amazon CloudWatch = Monitor EC2, CPU, memory (with agent), disk, application logs, metrics, alarms and dashboards.
	2. AWS CloudTrail    = Track API activities: who created, deleted, modified or accessed AWS resources.
	3. VPC Flow Logs     = Capture network traffic metadata, accepted/rejected connections, source and destination IPs.
	4. CloudWatch Logs   = Centralize and analyze application, system and security logs.


2. Threat Detection & Security Monitoring :-

	5. Amazon GuardDuty = Detect suspicious activity, compromised credentials, malware and unusual API calls.
	6. AWS Security Hub = Centralize security findings and assess security posture against standards.
	7. Amazon Detective = Investigate security incidents and understand relationships between suspicious activities.
	8. Amazon Inspector = Identify vulnerabilities in EC2, container images and supported Lambda workloads.
	9. Amazon Macie     = Discover and protect sensitive data, such as personally identifiable information (PII), in S3.

3. Network Security & Protection :-

	10. AWS Shield           = Protect applications against Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attacks.
	11. AWS WAF              = Protect web applications against SQL injection, cross-site scripting and unwanted web requests.
	12. AWS Network Firewall = Inspect and filter network traffic entering, leaving and moving through VPCs.
	13. AWS Firewall Manager = Centrally manage firewall policies across multiple AWS accounts.

